            "review_title": "Review at Quan Oc Xuan Anh",
            "review_text": "GlobalKuidaore\nAsia380 contributions\n0\nOur Favorite Seafood Place in Nha Trang\nMar 2018 • Couples\nWe eat here several times while we stay in Nha Trang for two months ever year. It was recommended by the pharmacy across the street. We tried a couple of other places on Thap Ba, but we like this place better. \n\nWe love their spicy surf clam soup. We like boiled (rather than sauteed) Mantis Shrimp, but we order it only when they have big ones. We’ve also had different kinds of shrimp and crab as well as clams and oysters. A lot of Vietnamese people seem to order clams and sea urchin here, but we don’t like the way they are cooked (grilled). We also like their stir-fried water spinach(kang kong) with lots of garlic.\n\nService isn’t good, as some reviewers said, but to us that’s the norm at most hole-in-the-wall places we eat at in Nha Trang and we don’t care as long as the food is good.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten March 10, 2018",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-11",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
