            "review_text": "Elizabeth K\n18 contributions\n1\nGreat seafood - eat here!\nJan 2018 • Couples\nThis is a great roadside seafood restaurant on 'seafood street' in Nha Trang. It is very busy and popular with locals - you pick your fresh seafood of choice by the kilo or 1/2 kilo from the range of buckets when oxygen being pumped through the water to keep the shellfish alive. You can choose how its cooked (BBQ, pan fried, steamed) but it will be suggested how best to have it. There is a nice lady (who speaks English) who takes the order and then you find a spot on the tiny blue chairs along the street and wait for your food. We had a 1/2 kilo of razor clams steamed with chilli and garlic and a 1/2 kilo of scallops bbq'ed with peanuts and spring onions on top. Both cost 100,000 vnd a piece and were AMAZING. This was plenty for us as we'd already had a couple of banh xeo (squid and prawn pancake-y type things) from the place opposite the Cham towers. Beers are cheap.\nIf you like seafood definitely give this place a try! Just remember prices are by weight and you should to ask the price of everything as you order.\nRead more\nWritten January 9, 2018",
            "rating": 1.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-11",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
