            "review_text": "Phuong Nhoc\n41 contributions\n0\nReasonable price with fresh good seafood\nJun 2017 • Family\nIt is more a street type restaurant with short distance from the centre. It has a veriety of seafood at very reasonable price, even for budget travellers. The staff are not so friendly and well trained so the service is sometimes a bit unorganized especially when they have many customers. Hygiene is also something of concern. The food is cooked just when ordered so you can enjoy the full taste of it. For me, fish is the best as you can have both fish porridge and grill with just 1 fish. Snails fried with coconut milk is also my favorite. So yummy!\nRead more\nWritten June 28, 2017",
