            "review_title": "Review at Quan Oc Xuan Anh",
            "review_text": "DRAJW\nMelbourne, Australia14 contributions\n0\nGreat local seafood joint. Be adventurous and eat here!\nMar 2015 • Couples\nThis is a seafood road side restaurant that caters almost entirely to locals. Don't be put off. \n\nCosts around $2 to catch a cab up here from downtown. All the cab drivers know where this is. It's popular with locals. Our resort staff were very impressed we were going here \"how did you know about this place? - it's our favourite seafood place...\"\n\nYou arrive and point to the type of seafood you want. There are lobsters, crabs, fish, oysters, snails, calamari etc etc. it was easy to get a price for what we wanted to eat from the mostly non English speaking staff. There didn't seem to be English menus. \n\nMost things seem to get bbq'd over coals but crab and a few other things were wok tossed in chilli and tamarind etc. \n\nYou sit on small plastic stools that you see all over the country with a table to eat off similar to most other road side stalls. There was an inside section of the restaurant that you can sit at if raining. \n\nAll our dishes were fresh and delicious. We are here for $7 per head and were full. \n\nNote they weren't open at lunch on a Friday when we first went - we came back at dinner and they were packed.\nRead more\nWritten March 10, 2015",
